CivScript v0.1 language notes

Lexical rules


One command per line.

Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.

Variable names start with a letter or underscore and then contain letters, digits, or underscores.

Numeric values must be finite JavaScript numbers.


Commands

Form	Meaning
SET name number	Assign a numeric variable
BEAM_MOMENT load span	Call Fortran backend for a simply supported beam under full-span UDL
DISPLAY	Print the last computed result

Current limitations

No arithmetic expressions in script files, strings, arrays, loops, functions, user-defined units, or general-purpose execution. Commands are parsed explicitly; script files are not evaluated as JavaScript.

  
